<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>About SIA</title>
    <link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.3/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css" rel="stylesheet">
    
    <style>
        
        body {
            background-color: rgb(7, 41, 82);
            color: white;
        }

        
        .heading-container {
            background-image: linear-gradient(rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2), rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5)), 
                              url('https://static0.simpleflyingimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2025/12/what-are-the-benefits-of-flying-singapore-airlines-first-class.jpg?w=1600&h=900&fit=crop');
            background-size: cover;
            background-position: center;
            height: 600px;
            width: 100%;
            display: flex;
            align-items: flex-end;
            justify-content: flex-start;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }

        .custom-table {
            background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
            border-collapse: separate;
            border-spacing: 0;
            border-radius: 10px;
            overflow: hidden;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

    <div class="heading-container p-4 p-md-5 mb-5">
        <div class="container-fluid px-0">
            <h1 class="display-3 fw-bold text-white text-start lh-sm m-0">
                Introduce <br> with the journey of SIA
            </h1>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="container my-5">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-12 text-center mb-4">
                <h2 class="fw-semibold border-bottom border-secondary pb-3">The Historical Flight Path of SIA</h2>
                <p class="text-light-50">Tracing the milestones from regional operator to a world-leading global carrier.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-12">
                <div class="table-responsive">
                    <table class="table table-dark align-middle custom-table m-0">
                        <thead class="table-light">
                            <tr>
                                <th scope="col" class="py-3 ps-4 text-dark" style="width: 15%;">Year</th>
                                <th scope="col" class="py-3 text-dark" style="width: 30%;">Milestone Event</th>
                                <th scope="col" class="py-3 pe-4 text-dark" style="width: 55%;">Key Accomplishments & Impact</th>
                            </tr>
                        </thead>
                        <tbody>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="fw-bold text-warning ps-4">1947</td>
                                <td><span class="badge bg-primary px-2 py-1">Inception</span> Malayan Airways Limited</td>
                                <td class="text-light pe-4">SIA's earliest roots begin with Malayan Airways Limited (MAL), which operated its maiden commercial flight connecting Singapore, Kuala Lumpur, Ipoh, and Penang.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="fw-bold text-warning ps-4">1966</td>
                                <td>Malaysia-Singapore Airlines (MSA)</td>
                                <td class="text-light pe-4">Following political transitions in the region, the airline was jointly owned by both governments and rebranded as MSA, rapidly expanding its network footprint.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="fw-bold text-warning ps-4">1972</td>
                                <td><span class="badge bg-success px-2 py-1">Birth of SIA</span> Official Incorporation</td>
                                <td class="text-light pe-4">MSA dissolved into two separate entities. Singapore Airlines (SIA) was officially formed, inheriting the international route network, the existing fleet of Boeing aircraft, and the Singapore headquarters.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="fw-bold text-warning ps-4">1973</td>
                                <td>Entering the Jumbo Jet Era</td>
                                <td class="text-light pe-4">SIA made history as the first airline in Southeast Asia to order Boeing 747 jumbo jets, cementing its commitment to long-haul, premium international travel.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="fw-bold text-warning ps-4">1981</td>
                                <td>Changi Airport Hub Hub Integration</td>
                                <td class="text-light pe-4">Operations officially moved to the newly opened, ultra-modern Singapore Changi Airport. This move provided SIA with a highly efficient base to drive massive global expansions.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="fw-bold text-warning ps-4">2000</td>
                                <td>Star Alliance Membership</td>
                                <td class="text-light pe-4">SIA officially joined Star Alliance, opening up shared networks, codeshare capabilities, and seamless international transit rewards for global passengers.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="fw-bold text-warning ps-4">2007</td>
                                <td><span class="badge bg-info text-dark px-2 py-1">World First</span> Aviation History with the A380</td>
                                <td class="text-light pe-4">SIA became the absolute global launch customer and first carrier in the world to fly the massive double-decker Airbus A380 passenger aircraft, debuting its iconic luxury Suites.</td>
                            </tr>
                            <tr>
                                <td class="fw-bold text-warning ps-4">2024 - 2026</td>
                                <td>Modern Mergers & Accolades</td>
                                <td class="text-light pe-4">Completed the Air India-Vistara merger securing a 25.1% stake in the expanded Air India. SIA continues to sweep Skytrax and Fortune awards, ranking consistently as the world's most admired airline.</td>
                            </tr>
                        </tbody>
                    </table>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.3/dist/js/bootstrap.bundle.min.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
